# Magnum's own directory. Only TWO things in here are
# shared: the specifications, and the project's own flows.
#
# v0.14.s — could .magnum simply be local and gitignored? Almost.
# Everything Magnum produces for itself — run records, the
# knowledge graph, analysis artifacts, the notes it leaves itself —
# is personal, disposable and was landing in the operator's checkout
# as day-one dirt, which is what blocked their first git pull.
#
# The exception is docs/. A ticket's specification is the ORDER the
# work was built from: it rides the ticket's branch, a reviewer opens
# one diff and sees what was promised beside what was delivered, and
# the implementation review fetches it from that branch over the API.
# Ignore it and every review fails with "no specification in the
# branch".
#
# v0.15.d9 — and flows/: the pipelines this project built for itself.
# A colleague who pulls must get them too, and the daemon reads them
# from the checkout it works in.
*
!.gitignore
!docs/
!docs/**
!flows/
!flows/**
!specs/
!specs/**
